CERTIFICATE OF INDEPENDENT TENDER DETERMINATION

I, the undersigned, in submitting the accompanying Letter of Tender to {procuring_entity_name} for: {tender_title} ({tender_reference}) in response to the request for tenders made by {tenderer_name} do hereby make the following statements that I certify to be true and complete in every respect:

1. I have read and I understand the contents of this Certificate;
2. I understand that the Tender will be disqualified if this Certificate is found not to be true and complete in every respect;
3. I am the authorized representative of the Tenderer with authority to sign this Certificate, and to submit the Tender on behalf of the Tenderer;
4. For the purposes of this Certificate and the Tender, I understand that the word "competitor" shall include any individual or organization, other than the Tenderer, whether or not affiliated with the Tenderer, who has been requested to submit a Tender in response to this request for tenders, or who could potentially submit a tender based on their qualifications, abilities or experience;
5. Independent-tender determination: {independent_tender_statement}
{competitor_disclosures_block}

Declarant: {declarant_name}, {declarant_title}
Postal address: {declarant_postal_address}
Place of residence: {declarant_place_of_residence}
Country of residence: {declarant_country_of_residence}
Certified at: {certified_at}

DECLARATION AND COMMITMENT TO THE CODE OF ETHICS

I, {declarant_name}, {declarant_title} of {tenderer_name}, declare that I have read and fully understood the contents of the Public Procurement and Asset Disposal Act and the Code of Ethics for persons participating in public procurement, and I make this solemn declaration conscientiously believing the same to be true.

I commit to comply with the applicable procurement legislation and Code of Ethics in respect of Tender No. {tender_reference} ({tender_title}) for {procuring_entity_name}.

FRAUD AND CORRUPTION APPENDIX ACKNOWLEDGED
{fraud_and_corruption_appendix}

Declarant: {declarant_name}, {declarant_title}
Certified at: {certified_at}

legal_records.appendix_body:
APPENDIX — FRAUD AND CORRUPTION

The Tenderer shall not engage in corrupt, fraudulent, collusive, coercive or obstructive practices. For the purposes of this Appendix:
(a) "corrupt practice" means the offering, giving, receiving, or soliciting of anything of value to influence the action of a public official in the procurement process or in contract execution;
(b) "fraudulent practice" means a misrepresentation of facts in order to influence a procurement process or the execution of a contract to the detriment of the Procuring Entity;
(c) "collusive practice" means a scheme or arrangement between two or more tenderers designed to establish tender prices at artificial, non-competitive levels;
(d) "coercive practice" means harming or threatening to harm persons or their property to influence their participation in a procurement process;
(e) "obstructive practice" means deliberately destroying, falsifying, altering or concealing evidence material to an investigation.

The Tenderer acknowledges that breach of these provisions may result in debarment, cancellation of the contract, and other remedies available in law.

